<Doc slug="run-a-server">
  <p>
    Most groups can use Zafe’s server. Run your own if you’d rather no outside operator
    sees when your members talk, want to look after its uptime yourself, or want to offer
    one to other groups. It holds no keys and can’t spend.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you start</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A Linux server you control: 1 vCPU and 1 GB of memory are enough.</li>
    <li>Docker with the Compose plugin.</li>
    <li>A domain name, with an A or AAAA record pointing at the server. Turn off any CDN proxy: the server needs the real connections, and a proxy would see every member’s address.</li>
    <li>Ports 80 and 443 open. Nothing else needs to be.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Set it up</h2>
  <p>The Compose file runs the server behind Caddy, which gets and renews its HTTPS certificate, plus a nightly backup.</p>
  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <li>
      Get the files:
      <pre><code>git clone --depth 1 {repo}
sudo cp -r zafe/infra/relay/vps /opt/zafe-relay
cd /opt/zafe-relay</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      Name the image and your domain in <code>.env</code>. The service is called
      <code>relay-testnet</code> for historical reasons; it serves mainnet vaults too.
      <pre><code>sudo tee .env &lt;&lt;'EOF'
RELAY_TESTNET_IMAGE=ghcr.io/zafe-cash/zafe-relay:main
RELAY_TESTNET_DOMAIN=relay.example.org
EOF
sudo install -d -o 10001 -g 10001 -m 700 /var/backups/zafe-relay/testnet</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
      Start it and check it answers:
      <pre><code>sudo docker compose up -d
curl https://relay.example.org/health      # ok</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Check it from a phone: on <strong>New vault</strong>, tap <strong>More options</strong>, <strong>Server</strong>, then <strong>Other address</strong>, and enter <code>relay.example.org</code>. <strong>Use this server</strong> turns on once it answers.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Make it private</h2>
  <p>
    By default anyone can create a vault on your server. With a create token, creating or
    restoring a vault needs it; joining, paying and everything else doesn’t.
  </p>
  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <li>
      Put a token in <code>secrets.env</code>, next to <code>compose.yml</code>, and restart:
      <pre><code>echo "ZAFE_RELAY_CREATE_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 24)" | sudo tee secrets.env &gt; /dev/null
sudo chmod 600 secrets.env
sudo docker compose up -d</code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>Give the group the address and token in one piece: <code>relay.example.org#&lt;token&gt;</code>. Pasted or scanned into <strong>Other address</strong>, it fills in the <strong>Create token</strong>.</li>
    <li>Members’ phones keep the token with the vault and in backups, since restoring the vault needs it. If it leaks, change it in <code>secrets.env</code> and give the group the new one.</li>
  </ol>
  <Shot
    name="docs_server_list"
    width={780}
    height={860}
    alt="Zafe's server list: relay.zafe.cash run by Zafe, and Other address set to relay.dao.org, with the line “No notifications” and an empty Create token field."
    caption="A private server in the app’s server list."
